window.bookSummaryJSON = "\"Delightfully funny, smart and sexy, this slow-burn romance features two fantastic lead characters and a lot of chemistry. Guaranteed to put a smile on your face!\" Jane Costello <p> <em>Hearts are set to race on the busiest night shift of the year…</em> </p> <p>Violet Winters is starting her first week of nights and she is petrified. She’s a straight-A student, but practising medicine on real people is another matter entirely. Seems like being a straight-talker can get you in hot water when it comes to patient care… With no one special to spend Christmas with, she signs herself up for the holiday night shift. How much damage could she possibly do?</p> <p>Dr Gus Jovic, on the other hand, is universally popular, famously unflappable in a crisis and appears to charm patients with ease. But Violet can't help but wonder … how come Mr Perfect is avoiding a Christmas at home too?</p> <p> <strong>Tropes:</strong> </p> <ul><li>Neurodivergent FMC</li><li>Workplace romance</li><li>Seasonal romcom</li><li>Forced proximity</li><li>Medical setting</li></ul> Authors and readers love <em>The Night Shift</em>: <p>'A <strong>delicious festive treat</strong> with a romance that truly sparkled. <strong>I defy anyone with a heartbeat not to fall in love with Violet and Gus. </strong>This is, without a doubt, Peach's best book to date' Jenni Keer</p> <p>'<em>The Night Shift </em>could almost be <strong>Beth O’Leary and Ali Hazelwood’s love child</strong>, except it’s pure Nancy Peach pedigree. <strong>Witty, clever and heartfelt</strong>, her writing absolutely drew me in and this is one of my favourite reads this year.' Julie Caplin</p> <p>⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐'<strong>Remember Dr Dreamy? Well, Hello Dr Gus Jovic</strong>. If you were ever a fan of <em>Grey’s Anatomy</em> or <em>ER</em> and the Britishness of <em>Green Wing</em>, then this is a must. Peach is sharp in her observations, smart in her insights, and <strong>this new story is just what the doctor ordered</strong>'</p> <p>⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ 'If <em>Grey’s Anatomy</em>, <em>The Pitt</em>, <em>ER</em>, and <em>Yours Truly</em> by Abby Jimenez had a baby, it would be <em>The Night Shift</em>. And honestly? That baby would be <strong>charming, chaotic, heartwarming, and a little bit neurospicy (in the best way)</strong>.If you love smart, quirky rom coms with big heart and even bigger personalities, this is the book for you'</p> <p>⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐Absolutely loved it! Especially being a nurse, I felt right at home observing the romance between Gus and Violet<strong>. It had me laughing out loud, kicking my feet with joy and holding back tears</strong>'</p> <p>⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ 'I’m not typically drawn to books with a hospital setting (too squeamish!), but I absolutely loved it. <strong>The romance was beautifully done</strong>'</p> <p>⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐'There was something <strong>absolutely captivating</strong> about reading a book from a neurodivergent perspective. <strong>This novel makes me wanna read more by the author!</strong>'</p> <p>⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐'Working in a non-clinical position within the NHS, I found <em>The Night Shift</em> to be<strong> a genuinely touching and uplifting read</strong> that shines a light on the emotional realities faced by healthcare professionals'</p> <p>⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐What an absolutely brilliant story. <strong>Nancy Peach gives us so much more than a romance;</strong> she paints a vivid portrait of the people behind the scrubs and the system they navigate daily'</p> <p>'Smart, tender and funny, <em>The Night Shift</em> is <strong>a total delight from start to finish.</strong> Nancy Peach has a gift for capturing the chaos and charm of real life, and <strong>I’d happily sign up for a night shift or ten with Dr. Gus</strong>!’ Kate Galloway, author of <em>Wild Swimming </em> </p> <p>'A <strong>sweet, sexy, and sincere romance</strong> with refreshing neurodiversity representation. <strong>The perfect tapestry of heart-wrenching emotion woven with heartwarming moments</strong>. Loved it.' Zoe Allison, author of <em>The Wedding Engagement </em> </p> <p>'<em>The Night Shift </em>is <strong>brimming with sexual chemistry and top-notch banter</strong>. A sparkling, slow-burn romance that will charm your socks off! I loved it!' Emma Rae, author of <em>Love Game</em> </p>"; 
